# pnpm settings are NOT configured here anymore.
#
# Since pnpm 11, `.npmrc` is only read for auth and registry settings. Every other
# pnpm setting (nodeLinker, hoistPattern, shamefullyHoist, ...) must live in
# `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, in camelCase. A `node-linker=hoisted` line here is dead:
# `pnpm config get node-linker` returns undefined and npm warns
# "Unknown project config node-linker".
#
# History: this repo used to declare `node-linker=hoisted` to force a flat
# node_modules. Original reason: the primary clone lives under OneDrive and was
# moved between folders; pnpm's absolute symlinks ended up dangling
# (ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND / UNKNOWN read) and OneDrive handles reparse points
# poorly. That reason still holds ONLY for the clone under OneDrive — worktrees
# outside it (C:\worktrees\*) run fine on pnpm 11's default `isolated` linker.
#
# `isolated` was kept on purpose: it leaves only declared dependencies at the
# root of node_modules, which is exactly what exposed the phantom dependency
# `allure-js-commons` (imported by tests/utils/decorators.ts without being in
# package.json). Going back to `hoisted` would mask that class of bug again. If
# the OneDrive clone needs the flat linker, set it there with
# `pnpm config set nodeLinker hoisted --location project` — not in this
# versioned file.
